<</nobr>>
10:15 PM. The apartment. The ritual   but tonight the ritual has a new step.

I stand in front of the bathroom mirror. The nose has settled fully. The bridge is sharp now   defined, narrow, running straight from the brow line to the tip in a clean profile that catches the overhead light (flicker, flicker, on) and channels it the way a finished surface channels light. The tip is soft. Angled. The Slope. The feature that Dr. Maren described as "the primary masculine tell" is gone, replaced by something that tells a different story.

I go to the desk. Wig on. Three minutes. VoxMorph calibrated. OBS loaded.

Now the change. I tilt the webcam down. Not much   an inch, maybe an inch and a half. The preview frame that has shown eyes-and-hair for three days now drops to include the nose. The new nose. The straight bridge and the soft tip and the proportion that Dr. Maren called "harmonizing."

Eyes. Lashes. Brows. Nose. Hair.

The crop line has fallen. The preview shows more of Ellie than any stream before   the upper two-thirds of a face that reads as feminine without question, without hesitation, without the half-second of gender-classification that the brain runs on every new face. The viewer seeing this thumbnail will think "girl" before they think anything else.

I angle the desk lamp. The warm gold catches the new nose   the bridge creating a clean line of highlight, the slope casting a soft shadow on the upper lip area, the geometry of the modification designed for exactly this: being seen on camera.

I check the preview one final time. The face in the rectangle is   closer. Closer to Ellie than it's ever been. Closer to the face reveal. Closer to the destination that the viewers have been building in their imaginations and that I've been building in a clinic four blocks away.

She looks real.

ElliePlayz   Live
Category: Just Chatting → Gunmetal Requiem
Viewers: 0

I look at the lens. Click "Go Live."


