:: day_5_24_other
<<set $day_step to 24>>
The apartment is dark. The fridge hums. The ceiling crack is up there   growing, always growing, but sharing the ceiling now with a number that passed four digits today and keeps climbing.

I lie on the mattress. Grey sheets. Thin comforter. The phone beside my head, Kira's red heart glowing in the notification bar, the RegenaForm app icon teal and patient beside it.

The numbers fade first. They always fade. The dashboard recedes, the followers count dissolving, the $1,048 becoming abstract in the way money becomes abstract when the screen is off and the body is horizontal and the brain shifts from calculating to wandering.

Kira fades second. Not completely   she doesn't fade completely, she never does   but the warmth of her settles into the background, the ambient temperature rather than the active flame. The homework is done. The red heart is sent. She said she'll wait. The Kira file closes partially, not locked, just resting.

What remains, in the dark, on the mattress, is the stranger.

She's been waiting. Behind the numbers and behind Kira and behind the nose and behind the stream and behind sophie1234's precise observations and behind the Floor 17 boss with eight arms and behind the bulgogi and behind everything that happened today   the stranger has been waiting in the room the body reserves for things the mind won't schedule.

The restaurant. The dark dress. The long hair catching red-gold light. The cheekbones that the RegenaForm catalog taught me to name   "High & Defined," the option that photographs beautifully. The lips   "Cupid's Bow," 450 dollars. The legs crossing, the fabric riding up, the line from ankle to thigh.

She's a composite now. The memory has degraded further   another day of distance between the observation and the recall, another layer of imagination deposited over the original impression. The stranger I saw for three seconds is becoming the stranger I'm building in my head, detail by invented detail, the way I'm building Ellie feature by feature. Both are constructions. Both are real in the way that constructed things can be real   functional, inhabitable, responsive to attention.

My hand moves. The familiar route. Under the comforter. Under the waistband.

The stranger's body. Reconstructed from fragments and filled in with desire. The breasts I couldn't classify   C, D, the letters that floated last night and float again tonight, the alphabet of a body I'm learning in theory while constructing another body in practice. The waist. The hips. The dress sliding off a shoulder, the leather jacket already gone, the skin beneath   smooth and warm in the imagination, the specific warmth of a body that exists only in the gap between what I saw and what I want.

The letters haunt me differently tonight. B. C. D. They're not just the stranger's measurements anymore   they're entries in a catalog I've read, options in a system I'm navigating, prices in a tier I told myself was irrelevant. Tier 5. Breasts. A through G+. The page I scrolled past in the RegenaForm app because it doesn't apply, because I'm only doing Tier 1, because the face is the project and the body is someone else's territory.

But the letters know my name. The letters have been sitting in my peripheral vision since I first opened the lookbook in the waiting room, since Dr. Maren's digital overlay showed a face that could be anything, since Lina's impossible body demonstrated what "anything" looks like when it's fully assembled.

The rhythm is steady. The images cycle   the stranger's body, the letter-classification game, the dress coming off, the skin, the shape I can't name with confidence. C. Maybe D. The question that has no answer because the data is insufficient and the imagination is too generous and the body doesn't care about accuracy, only function.

The peak. The arch. The release   a shudder that carries less weight than last night's version because the emotional load is lighter (Kira texted back, Marcus came over, the nose is done, the homework is submitted) but the physical load is the same, the same wave, the same white room for three seconds, the same emptying.

Then the refilling. The white room restocks.

Sophie1234. "The mystery is the product." "Natural or sculpted?" "Well played. In every sense."

The sentences sit in the post-orgasmic quiet with a clarity they didn't have during the stream. Sophie saw the construction. Sophie identified the brow sculpting in her first five minutes. Sophie gave framing advice that was technically correct. Sophie said "goodnight" with a period and a precision that matched Dr. Maren's clinical attention.

Who is sophie1234?

The question joins the others   the stranger's cup size, the homework's other half, the nose credit due in six days, the lips at $400, the jawline at $600. Questions without answers, accumulating in the dark, each one a weight on a mattress that's already holding a person who weighs more than he used to because the person he's becoming has more pieces.

I clean up. Tissue. Pull the comforter to my chin. The phone glows beside my head   Kira's red heart, the RegenaForm icon, the ElliePlayz dashboard in the browser tab I never close.

Tomorrow. Morning stream. Ellie with the nose. The numbers climbing. The crop line holding. The face reveal getting closer. The lips next, maybe. The jawline after that. The cathedral, stone by stone and sophie1234. Watching. Paying attention to different things.

I close my eyes. The fridge hums. The crack grows. The face grows. The audience grows. The secret grows.

I sleep and I dream about two faces   the stranger's and Ellie's   merging and separating and merging again in a mirror that shows both at once, and a voice in the dream that says "natural or sculpted?" and I can't tell which face the question is for.

